  "limitations": [
    "The finite model assumes unique identities and atomic immutable uploads; no Rust refinement or composition/liveness theorem",
    "No physical collector is active; checkpoint, orphan and retained-reference reclamation remain open",
    "References do not reserve global/tenant physical credit themselves; the production controller must admit and retain charges for uncertain uploads",
    "Partial reads require index block integrity; only complete bounded blob reads verify the full SHA-256 digest",
    "The 8 MiB cache setting is weighted entry capacity, not whole-process RSS; namespaces, buffers and concurrent callers need aggregate admission",
    "Deterministic clocks and stopped writers do not qualify live ownership, autoscaling or a production timing contract",
    "No serving API, tenant lifecycle, transaction-receipt composition or production dependency/toolchain adoption",
    "Small debug timing samples do not establish sustained throughput or latency percentiles; MinIO is not AWS",
    "The experimental payload encoding changes without a mixed-format migration path; use fresh buckets"
  ],
